  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 157 PM EDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nAs the long term sets up, a strengthening ridge will be building in \nfor the weekend. Chances for afternoon storms will start to decline, \nwhile the risk for excessive heat ramps up. By Friday, most of the \nCWA can expect apparent temperatures in the triple digits with the \neastern part of the forecast area reaching Heat Advisory criteria. \nWe'll need to keep an eye on temps over the next couple of days, but \nif you have plans for this coming weekend, keep the heat in mind. \n\nThat's what we do know. Now for what we don't...\n\nOver the next couple of days we'll be transitioning into NW flow. \nThis kind of pattern is notorious for letting MCS' make a big run \nacross half the country and end up on our doorstep. Long term models \nstruggle to pick these out from the noise, and as a result we'll \njust need to wait and see how the ridge sets up over the next few \ndays. These ridge riders also have a habit of interrupting \nforecasted high temperatures with the introduction of rain, making \nthe long term forecast a bit on the tricky side.",
